# Commands

Run each with `uv run {{ project_name }} …`. `--help` on any command shows its options. This app's own commands
come first; the rest are duckkit's standard commands (the same in every app made from the scaffold).

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ingest <files>` | load data into the database (this app's own) |
| `status` | what the database holds, and the contract check |
| `sql "<SELECT>"` | one read-only SELECT on a snapshot (prefer the contract views) |
| `app [name] [--tailnet]{% if demo_data %} [--demo]{% endif %}` | serve an app on localhost: `app` (:{{ app_port }}){% for a in extra_apps %}, `{{ a.name }}` (:{{ a.port }}){% endfor %} |
{%- if motherduck %}
| `publish [--to md:<name>] [--dry-run] [--check]` | the contract views to MotherDuck (`md:{{ motherduck_db }}`); `--check` compares |
{%- endif %}
{%- if backup %}
| `backup` | a verified Parquet snapshot in the backup folder |
| `backups` | the snapshots, oldest first |
| `restore <snapshot> [--to <file>]` | a new database from a snapshot (never overwrites) |
{%- endif %}
| `privacy-check` | fail if a file git would commit holds personal data |
| `doctor [--remote]` | whether the repo is in step with the scaffold |
